.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.csv
# ...but NOT the committed research provenance artifacts. The blanket *.csv above
# silently ate four fixtures that tools/overnight_gap_risk_study.py declares
# SHA-256 hashes for (entry_bar_5m_ordering_2026.csv, entry_bar_1m_resolution_2026.csv,
# tqqq_corporate_actions_2010_2026.csv, qqq_distributions_2010_2026.csv). Their JSON
# sibling in the same directory and the same commit survived, because only the .csv
# extension matched — `git add` on an ignored path is a silent no-op. Those four
# fixtures are the sole evidence behind ~32% of RESEARCH_WEB.md and cannot be
# regenerated offline. Committing them is the one action that restores it.
!docs/research/data/*.csv
.DS_Store
venv
venv/
# Both forms on purpose. `venv/` alone matches only a DIRECTORY, so a symlink
# named `venv` — which is exactly what a scratch worktree needs, since the real
# venv is untracked — slips past it and can be committed by `git add -A`. When
# that lands, checkout replaces the real venv/ with a self-referential symlink
# and destroys the interpreter the trader runs from.
*.egg-info/
experiments.jsonl
sweep_results_*.json
live/state.db
state.db
local_ops/
local_logs/
.ibkr-paper.env
*.ibkr-paper.env

# Raw databases — never commit; export sanitized JSON instead
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Runtime / operational artifacts
*.pid
*.tmp
data/live_runs/tmp_*/
local_backups/
local_runtime/
# Strategy-funnel offline research output (survivor/rejection cards)
data/funnel_runs/
# Graphify ingestion output + the bridge's suggestions (never auto-committed)
graphify-out/
data/graphify_suggestions/
# Screener caches (tools/screener_lab.py + tools/stock_screener.py). Regenerable by
# refresh/fetch, and they churn every run — a snapshot is a CACHE, not a provenance
# artifact, and the distinction is the whole subject of tools/data_cache.py. The sibling
# *.csv panels here were already covered by the blanket rule at the top; these are JSON
# and were not, so `git add -A` would have committed vendor rows on every refresh.
data/cache/screener_snapshot.json
data/cache/sp500_universe.json
# The StockTwits ring cursor — run state, not data.
data/cache/stocktwits_cursor.json
data/screener/fundamentals.json
# Same reasoning: closes are refetched, they churn every session, and the Pages build
# pulls its own. A price cache is a CACHE, not a provenance artifact.
data/screener/prices.json
# Derived from prices.json, regenerated when it changes. Output, not a record.
data/screener/concentration.json
# Same: regenerated from prices.json whenever it changes. Output, not a record.
data/screener/channel_stats.json
data/screener/bucket_lab.json
# Local tone-ledger residue. The CANONICAL ledger lives on the tone-ledger branch, written
# by CI; local and Pi runs keep their own rows on disk and must not show as untracked noise
# or sneak onto development.
data/tone_ledger/

# Static GitHub Pages export (built in CI by .github/workflows/pages.yml)
_site/

# Coverage artifacts (CI/dev only — see .github/workflows/test.yml)
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# The pre-3.11 venv, kept until the rebuild is trusted. Never a commit.
venv-py39-backup/
